== a plain single quote lists the markers:
'ZQdir_marker/
'ZQcommand_marker
'ZQmarker_file
== an ANSI C quote lists the same markers:
$'ZQdir_marker/
$'ZQcommand_marker
$'ZQmarker_file
== an ANSI C escape resolves to the decoded name:
$'ZQdir_marker/\x5aQinner'
== an ANSI C quote completes a command name:
$'ZQcommand_marker'
== an ANSI C quote after a directory keeps the prefix:
ZQdir_marker/$'ZQinner'
== a doubled dollar sign offers nothing, the process id prefix matches no file:
== a tripled dollar sign offers nothing, the process id prefix matches no file:
== a locale quote lists the same markers:
$"ZQdir_marker/
$"ZQcommand_marker
$"ZQmarker_file
== an escaped quote keeps the locale quoted word open and matches no file:
== a locale quote completes a command name:
$"ZQcommand_marker"
== a locale quote after a directory keeps the prefix:
ZQdir_marker/$"ZQinner"
== a doubled dollar sign before a locale quote offers nothing:
